# Dogan Android → local Docker API (Mobile MCP)

**Goal:** Confirm `com.dogan` on AVD `Dogan_UI_API33` can auth/health-check against host Docker `dogan-api` on `:8080`.

## Steps
1. Ensure stack healthy: `docker ps` shows `dogan-api` healthy; `http://localhost:8080/dogan/api/v1/health` → 200.
2. Start AVD: `%LOCALAPPDATA%\Android\Sdk\emulator\emulator.exe -avd Dogan_UI_API33 -gpu auto` (adb serial often `emulator-5556`).
3. Put `platform-tools` on PATH (bare `adb` may be missing).
4. Mobile MCP: `mobile_list_available_devices` → device id `Dogan_UI_API33`; launch `com.dogan`.
5. Connectivity settings → set API URL to `10.0.2.2:8080` (emulator alias for host loopback), stream URL to `http://10.0.2.2:8889` (host MediaMTX WHIP/WHEP), user/pass `admin`/`admin`, tap connect (unverified (post-migration)).
6. Pass: UI shows `API: Connected`, ping ms, button `CONNECTED`. Optional network proof: `adb shell` + `nc 10.0.2.2 8080` HTTP GET `/dogan/api/v1/health` → 200; confirm MediaMTX path `device-*` ready for a WHIP publish (unverified (post-migration)).

## Gotchas
- App defaults are remote `dogan-api.xaigrok.ir:443` and `dogan-media.xaigrok.ir:443` — hub shows DISCONNECTED until local host/port set (unverified (post-migration)).
- Use `10.0.2.2`, not `localhost`/`127.0.0.1`, unless you also `adb reverse tcp:8080 tcp:8080`.
- Cleartext allowed via `network_security_config` (`cleartextTrafficPermitted=true`).
- Emulator image has no `curl`/`wget`; use `nc` for HTTP probes.
- Mobile MCP `DPAD_END` unsupported — clear fields with BACKSPACE/`adb shell input` instead.

## What didn't work
- Assuming default API URL talks to local Docker — it points at production host.
- `curl`/`wget` from emulator shell — not installed on this AVD system image.
